      "text": "To find the greatest possible value of ( x ) that is a positive multiple of (3) and satisfies ( x^3 < 1000 ), we proceed as follows:\n\n1. First, we determine the maximum integer value of ( x ), which is obtained by taking the cube root of (1000) and rounding it down to the nearest integer. This can be represented as:\n   [\n   text{{max_integer}} = lceil 1000^{1/3} rceil\n   ]\n   where ( lceil cdot rceil ) denotes the ceiling function, which rounds a number up to the nearest integer.\n\n2. Next, we check if this maximum integer is a multiple of (3). If it is not, we reduce ( text{{max_integer}} ) by one to ensure it remains a multiple of (3).\n\n3. Finally, we verify whether the cube of (text{{max_integer}}) is less than (1000). If it is, then (text{{max_integer}}) is our answer; otherwise, we continue reducing (text{{max_integer}}) by one until the condition is satisfied.\n\nBy following these steps, we ensure that we find the greatest multiple of (3) that is also less than (1000) when cubed. The answer is (text{{max_integer}}).",
